<% content_for :title, "Cognitive Distortions | Bipolar Sober" %>

<main class="toolbox-cd-page">

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="toolbox-cd-hero">
    <div class="toolbox-cd-hero-content">

      <p class="toolbox-cd-eyebrow">
        BIPOLAR SOBER / TOOLBOX / COGNITIVE DISTORTIONS
      </p>

      <h1>
        <span>YOUR BRAIN</span>
        <span>IS TALKING</span>
        <span>SHIT.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="toolbox-cd-intro">
        A THOUGHT CAN FEEL TRUE<br>
        WITHOUT ACTUALLY BEING TRUE.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- INTRO -->
  <section class="cd-section cd-section-pink">

    <div class="cd-section-number">
      01 / WHAT THE FUCK IS THIS?
    </div>

    <div class="cd-section-content">

      <h2>
        YOUR FIRST<br>
        THOUGHT ISN'T<br>
        ALWAYS A FACT.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Cognitive distortions are patterns of thinking that can twist
        the way we interpret ourselves, other people, and what's happening
        around us.
      </p>

      <p>
        They're convincing because they don't usually arrive sounding
        ridiculous. They arrive sounding like the obvious explanation.
      </p>

      <div class="cd-callout">
        <p>
          YOUR BRAIN SAID IT.<br>
          THAT DOESN'T MAKE IT EVIDENCE.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- THE PROCESS -->
  <section class="cd-section cd-section-yellow">

    <div class="cd-section-number">
      02 / THE PROCESS
    </div>

    <div class="cd-section-content">

      <h2>
        CATCH IT.<br>
        QUESTION IT.<br>
        CHECK IT.
      </h2>

      <div class="cd-process">

        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>CATCH IT.</h3>
          <p>What did I just tell myself?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>NAME IT.</h3>
          <p>Is there a cognitive distortion hiding in there?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>CHECK IT.</h3>
          <p>What evidence actually supports this thought?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <h3>CHALLENGE IT.</h3>
          <p>Is there another explanation that also fits the facts?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>05</span>
          <h3>REWRITE IT.</h3>
          <p>What would a more accurate thought sound like?</p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- ALL OR NOTHING -->
  <section class="cd-section cd-section-purple">

    <div class="cd-section-number">
      03 / ALL-OR-NOTHING THINKING
    </div>

    <div class="cd-section-content">

      <h2>
        PERFECT<br>
        OR TOTAL<br>
        FUCKING FAILURE.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Everything becomes one extreme or the other.
        Success or failure. Good or bad. Sober forever or completely fucked.
      </p>

      <div class="cd-example">
        <p class="cd-example-label">THE THOUGHT</p>
        <p>"I fucked this up, so I've ruined everything."</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cd-example">
        <p class="cd-example-label">CHECK IT</p>
        <p>
          Did one mistake actually erase everything that happened before it?
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="cd-example">
        <p class="cd-example-label">TRY INSTEAD</p>
        <p>
          "I fucked something up. Now I have to decide what I do next."
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- CATASTROPHIZING -->
  <section class="cd-section cd-section-black">

    <div class="cd-section-number">
      04 / CATASTROPHIZING
    </div>

    <div class="cd-section-content">

      <h2>
        WELL,<br>
        OBVIOUSLY<br>
        WE'RE DOOMED.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Your brain skips past every ordinary possibility and heads
        straight for the worst possible ending.
      </p>

      <div class="cd-example">
        <p class="cd-example-label">THE THOUGHT</p>
        <p>"This happened, so everything is about to fall apart."</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cd-example">
        <p class="cd-example-label">ASK</p>
        <p>
          What do I actually know right now — and what am I predicting?
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- MIND READING -->
  <section class="cd-section cd-section-pink">

    <div class="cd-section-number">
      05 / MIND READING
    </div>

    <div class="cd-section-content">

      <h2>
        APPARENTLY<br>
        YOU'RE FUCKING<br>
        PSYCHIC NOW.
      </h2>

      <p>
        You decide what somebody else thinks or feels without actually
        having evidence.
      </p>

      <div class="cd-example">
        <p class="cd-example-label">THE THOUGHT</p>
        <p>"They think I'm a disaster."</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cd-example">
        <p class="cd-example-label">ASK</p>
        <p>
          Did they actually say that, or did my brain write their dialogue for them?
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- FORTUNE TELLING -->
  <section class="cd-section cd-section-yellow">

    <div class="cd-section-number">
      06 / FORTUNE TELLING
    </div>

    <div class="cd-section-content">

      <h2>
        YOU DON'T<br>
        KNOW WHAT<br>
        HAPPENS NEXT.
      </h2>

      <p>
        You predict an outcome and start reacting emotionally
        as though it has already happened.
      </p>

      <div class="cd-example">
        <p class="cd-example-label">THE THOUGHT</p>
        <p>"They're going to reject me anyway."</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cd-example">
        <p class="cd-example-label">ASK</p>
        <p>
          Is this something I know, or something I'm afraid might happen?
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- EMOTIONAL REASONING -->
  <section class="cd-section cd-section-purple">

    <div class="cd-section-number">
      07 / EMOTIONAL REASONING
    </div>

    <div class="cd-section-content">

      <h2>
        I FEEL IT.<br>
        THEREFORE<br>
        IT'S TRUE.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Feelings are real. But a feeling is not automatically proof
        that the story attached to it is accurate.
      </p>

      <div class="cd-example">
        <p class="cd-example-label">THE THOUGHT</p>
        <p>"I feel hopeless, so this situation must actually be hopeless."</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cd-example">
        <p class="cd-example-label">ASK</p>
        <p>
          What am I feeling — and separately, what do I actually know?
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- SHOULD STATEMENTS -->
  <section class="cd-section cd-section-black">

    <div class="cd-section-number">
      08 / SHOULD STATEMENTS
    </div>

    <div class="cd-section-content">

      <h2>
        SHOULD.<br>
        MUST.<br>
        SUPPOSED TO.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Rigid rules about how you or other people are "supposed" to behave
        can turn disappointment into shame, guilt, resentment, or anger.
      </p>

      <div class="cd-example">
        <p class="cd-example-label">THE THOUGHT</p>
        <p>"I should have my shit together by now."</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cd-example">
        <p class="cd-example-label">ASK</p>
        <p>
          According to fucking whom?
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- LABELING -->
  <section class="cd-section cd-section-pink">

    <div class="cd-section-number">
      09 / LABELING
    </div>

    <div class="cd-section-content">

      <h2>
        YOU DID<br>
        SOMETHING.<br>
        YOU AREN'T IT.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Labeling takes a behavior, mistake, diagnosis, or experience
        and turns it into your entire identity.
      </p>

      <div class="cd-example">
        <p class="cd-example-label">THE THOUGHT</p>
        <p>"I failed, so I'm a failure."</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cd-example">
        <p class="cd-example-label">TRY INSTEAD</p>
        <p>
          "Something went badly. That's information about what happened,
          not a complete definition of me."
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- DISCOUNTING POSITIVES -->
  <section class="cd-section cd-section-yellow">

    <div class="cd-section-number">
      10 / DISCOUNTING THE POSITIVE
    </div>

    <div class="cd-section-content">

      <h2>
        NOTHING<br>
        FUCKING<br>
        COUNTS.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Something goes right and your brain immediately explains why
        it doesn't count.
      </p>

      <div class="cd-example">
        <p class="cd-example-label">THE THOUGHT</p>
        <p>"Yeah, I did it, but it wasn't that hard."</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cd-example">
        <p class="cd-example-label">ASK</p>
        <p>
          If somebody else did this, would I dismiss it this quickly?
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- PERSONALIZATION -->
  <section class="cd-section cd-section-purple">

    <div class="cd-section-number">
      11 / PERSONALIZATION
    </div>

    <div class="cd-section-content">

      <h2>
        SOMEHOW<br>
        EVERYTHING<br>
        IS YOUR FAULT.
      </h2>

      <p>
        You take responsibility for things that aren't entirely
        within your control.
      </p>

      <div class="cd-example">
        <p class="cd-example-label">ASK</p>
        <p>
          What part of this actually belongs to me?
          What belongs to somebody else?
          What belongs to circumstances nobody controlled?
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- OVERGENERALIZATION -->
  <section class="cd-section cd-section-black">

    <div class="cd-section-number">
      12 / OVERGENERALIZATION
    </div>

    <div class="cd-section-content">

      <h2>
        ONE THING<br>
        BECOMES<br>
        EVERYTHING.
      </h2>

      <p>
        One bad experience becomes evidence for a giant rule about your life.
      </p>

      <div class="cd-example">
        <p class="cd-example-label">THE THOUGHT</p>
        <p>"This always happens to me."</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cd-example">
        <p class="cd-example-label">LOOK FOR</p>
        <p>
          Always. Never. Everyone. Nobody. Everything. Nothing.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p>
        Absolute words are a good clue that your brain may have taken
        one piece of evidence and gotten a little fucking ambitious.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- FILTER -->
  <section class="cd-section cd-section-pink">

    <div class="cd-section-number">
      13 / MENTAL FILTER
    </div>

    <div class="cd-section-content">

      <h2>
        TEN THINGS<br>
        WENT RIGHT.<br>
        GUESS WHICH ONE YOU REMEMBER.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Your attention locks onto the negative piece of an experience
        and filters out everything that doesn't fit it.
      </p>

      <div class="cd-example">
        <p class="cd-example-label">ASK</p>
        <p>
          What information am I leaving out because it doesn't match
          how I currently feel?
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- RECOVERY -->
  <section class="cd-section cd-section-yellow">

    <div class="cd-section-number">
      14 / RECOVERY
    </div>

    <div class="cd-section-content">

      <h2>
        WATCH THE<br>
        PERMISSION<br>
        SLIP.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Distorted thinking can become especially convincing when your brain
        wants permission to do something impulsive or return to an old behavior.
      </p>

      <div class="cd-permission-list">

        <p>"JUST THIS ONCE."</p>
        <p>"I CAN HANDLE IT NOW."</p>
        <p>"I ALREADY FUCKED UP, SO WHO CARES?"</p>
        <p>"I DESERVE THIS."</p>
        <p>"NOTHING BAD WILL HAPPEN THIS TIME."</p>

      </div>

      <p>
        Write the thought down. Read it back.
        If you can, say it out loud.
      </p>

      <p>
        Sometimes a thought that sounded incredibly convincing inside
        your head looks a whole lot different once it's sitting in front of you.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- PUT IT ON TRIAL -->
  <section class="cd-section cd-section-purple">

    <div class="cd-section-number">
      15 / PUT IT ON TRIAL
    </div>

    <div class="cd-section-content">

      <h2>
        SHOW ME<br>
        THE FUCKING<br>
        EVIDENCE.
      </h2>

      <div class="cd-trial">

        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <p>What is the thought?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <p>What facts support it?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <p>What facts don't support it?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <p>Am I assuming something I can't actually know?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>05</span>
          <p>What would I tell somebody else who had this thought?</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>06</span>
          <p>What is a more accurate version of the thought?</p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- ENDING -->
  <section class="cd-ending">

    <p class="cd-ending-small">
      YOU DON'T HAVE TO BELIEVE EVERYTHING YOUR BRAIN PRODUCES.
    </p>

    <h2>
      THINK IT.<br>
      QUESTION IT.<br>
      THEN DECIDE.
    </h2>

    <p>
      The goal isn't positive thinking.
      It's more accurate fucking thinking.
    </p>

    <%= link_to "← BACK TO TOOLBOX",
        toolbox_path,
        class: "cd-back-link" %>

  </section>

</main>